WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:02.035
Well, let me move on to Evan Gershkovich,
of course

00:00:02.068 --> 00:00:03.336
The Wall Street Journal reporter

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:07.707
who has been arrested and detained
in Russia on espionage charges.

00:00:08.008 --> 00:00:10.577
The administration has called these claims
ridiculous.

00:00:10.577 --> 00:00:14.280
Is in the process right now
trying to get a console visit with Evan.

00:00:14.514 --> 00:00:17.250
Has any
anything developed on that front yet?

00:00:17.984 --> 00:00:19.185
Sadly, no, Brianna.

00:00:19.185 --> 00:00:23.456
We have not been able to achieve consular
access and nobody from our embassy

00:00:23.957 --> 00:00:25.392
has been able to meet with him.

00:00:25.392 --> 00:00:28.561
We are continuing to work on that,
of course, and will

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:32.499
until we can get that consular access
to ascertain for ourselves

00:00:32.499 --> 00:00:36.302
how he's doing and make sure that
that we have that connection.

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:37.404
But no, we haven't.

00:00:37.404 --> 00:00:39.506
We haven't been able to gain access to him
at this time.

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:42.575
So there's no engagement with Evan,
no update

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:44.944
or status as to where he is
and how he is doing?

00:00:45.612 --> 00:00:46.446
I'm afraid not.

00:00:46.446 --> 00:00:49.115
I mean, we're we're doing the best
we can to get information

00:00:49.416 --> 00:00:52.685
from the Russian government,
obviously, as much as we can.

00:00:53.153 --> 00:00:56.423
And we have been in touch with the family
through the State Department.

00:00:56.923 --> 00:00:59.359
And we will continue
those lines of communication

00:00:59.492 --> 00:01:02.829
But right now, I just don't have much to
to update you on.

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:05.865
Of course, we are thinking about
his family and his colleagues right now.

00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:09.135
The FSB in their statement said that Mr.

00:01:09.369 --> 00:01:13.239
Kovac is, quote, suspected of spying in
the interests of the American government.

00:01:13.239 --> 00:01:15.075
And this is what really struck me, John.

00:01:15.075 --> 00:01:19.045
A Kremlin spokesperson and press
secretary, Dmitry Peskov, said that

00:01:19.045 --> 00:01:21.481
he was, quote, caught red handed.

00:01:21.481 --> 00:01:25.452
These are very provocative
and I would say deliberate words.

00:01:25.819 --> 00:01:26.486
I can't

00:01:26.486 --> 00:01:30.723
imagine that this would not have happened
without the sign off of Vladimir Putin.

00:01:30.824 --> 00:01:32.759
Do you agree with that assessment?

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:34.194
We can't delink.

00:01:34.194 --> 00:01:36.696
We can't specifically link Mr.

00:01:36.696 --> 00:01:38.331
Putin to to this arrest.

00:01:38.331 --> 00:01:42.302
That said, he, as you well
know, has really,

00:01:42.869 --> 00:01:46.906
really clamped down on independent media
reporting in Russia

00:01:47.574 --> 00:01:50.410
and just shutting down outlets,
kicking some out.

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:54.047
I mean, it's it's a very,
very tough environment for any kind of

00:01:54.047 --> 00:01:56.816
independent,
independent journalism to to occur.

00:01:57.350 --> 00:02:01.387
So he has certainly set the conditions
where it's very difficult

00:02:01.821 --> 00:02:04.457
for free and independent reporters
to actually do their job.

00:02:04.457 --> 00:02:06.926
And just to put a fine point on it,
you didn't ask, but

00:02:07.861 --> 00:02:10.497
the claims, the espionage
claims against Mr.

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:12.699
Gersh, which are absolutely ludicrous.

00:02:13.199 --> 00:02:15.602
He was a working journalist
for The Wall Street Journal.

00:02:15.935 --> 00:02:17.904
And we want to see him released. Yeah.

00:02:17.904 --> 00:02:19.472
And the administration noted yesterday

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:21.975
they call these claims
Karine Jean-Pierre called them ridiculous.

00:02:22.509 --> 00:02:26.212
I know that the State Department
is in its process, which is routine

00:02:26.212 --> 00:02:30.950
when an American is detained to
to get to the actual words and being able

00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:34.988
to label this wrongfully detained,
where does that process stand?

00:02:35.955 --> 00:02:37.891
I would
have to refer you to the state department.

00:02:37.891 --> 00:02:40.160
They do have a process
that they put in place

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:42.896
when when we have Americans
detained overseas where they

00:02:43.163 --> 00:02:45.031
take a look at the circumstances.

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:47.500
And I don't really know where they are
in that process.

00:02:47.834 --> 00:02:50.637
It is very much driven
by individual cases.

00:02:50.637 --> 00:02:54.474
So it's not driven by a specific timeline
necessarily.

00:02:54.841 --> 00:02:57.944
It's really driven by, you know,
taking a look at each case individually.

00:02:57.944 --> 00:03:01.381
And they'll do that and they'll do that
in the appropriate manner.

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:07.520
We're sure that in the meantime, it's
very clear that from everything

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:10.924
we've been able to glean that he was
simply picked up for being a reporter.

00:03:11.191 --> 00:03:15.261
And again, in a country where being
a reporter can be a very dangerous thing.

00:03:15.728 --> 00:03:18.431
And we want to see him released
We want to see him released right away

00:03:18.431 --> 00:03:18.965
immediately.

00:03:18.965 --> 00:03:21.534
That's he does not belong to be detained

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:24.671
for for doing the job of a reporter
in a foreign country.

00:03:25.038 --> 00:03:28.141
Let me read to you what his employer
The Wall Street Journal has said

00:03:28.141 --> 00:03:31.811
in their editorial and what they believe
is the government's duty now in response.

00:03:32.145 --> 00:03:36.849
They called his detainment another example
of Russia taking a journal hostage.

00:03:36.883 --> 00:03:39.519
Thuggish leaders
keep doing thuggish things

00:03:39.519 --> 00:03:41.221
if they think they will pay no price.

00:03:41.221 --> 00:03:45.158
Expelling Russia's ambassador to the U.S.,
as well as all Russian journalists,

00:03:45.158 --> 00:03:48.962
would be the minimum
to expect the US government's first duty

00:03:48.962 --> 00:03:51.331
is to protect its citizens,
and too many governments

00:03:51.331 --> 00:03:55.268
now believe that they can arrest
and imprison Americans with impunity.

00:03:55.735 --> 00:03:59.606
President Biden was asked just today
if he plans to expel

00:03:59.872 --> 00:04:01.441
Russian journalists or diplomats.

00:04:01.441 --> 00:04:03.910
He said there are
no plans right now. Why not?

00:04:04.911 --> 00:04:07.447
We are taking a look at this case
obviously very closely.

00:04:07.447 --> 00:04:12.151
Our focus right
now, Bianna, is getting Evan out of there,

00:04:12.151 --> 00:04:15.588
getting getting him released
and working towards getting him released.

00:04:15.588 --> 00:04:17.857
And so that's
where the focus is right now.

00:04:17.857 --> 00:04:20.460
And I don't have anything to add
to what the president said in terms

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:22.629
of any consequences
that will come from this.

00:04:22.629 --> 00:04:24.998
I think it's important
to remember a couple of things.

00:04:25.031 --> 00:04:27.300
Number one,
this is not a new tactic for Mr.

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:27.967
Putin.

00:04:28.201 --> 00:04:33.172
He has he has detained American citizens
and citizens from other countries

00:04:33.506 --> 00:04:36.809
in a routine way on many times
sham charges.

00:04:37.477 --> 00:04:38.278
That's number one.

00:04:38.278 --> 00:04:42.682
Number two, President Biden never forgets
Americans that are detained overseas.

00:04:42.682 --> 00:04:44.851
He has a whole team
here at the State Department

00:04:44.851 --> 00:04:48.021
at the National Security Council
dedicated to getting those folks home.

00:04:48.221 --> 00:04:49.789
And we're going to do that in Evan's case.

00:04:49.789 --> 00:04:52.725
We're going to work just as hard for Evan
as we are for everybody else.

00:04:53.026 --> 00:04:54.060
But each case has got to be

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:56.496
looked at individually.
The last thing I'll say here is

00:04:56.763 --> 00:04:59.265
this is not the time for Americans
to be in Russia.

00:04:59.265 --> 00:05:02.702
If you're in Russia now,
whether it's on business or leisure,

00:05:02.769 --> 00:05:04.771
whatever kind of travel
you need to leave now.

00:05:04.771 --> 00:05:05.738
This is not a good place

00:05:05.738 --> 00:05:08.741
for you to be in Russia,
even if you are a working journalist.

00:05:09.142 --> 00:05:12.512
Russia is a is a hostile environment
for American citizens right now,

00:05:12.845 --> 00:05:14.113
and it's time to go if you're there.

00:05:14.113 --> 00:05:14.747
So as you know,

00:05:14.747 --> 00:05:15.682
there are several

00:05:15.682 --> 00:05:18.718
international journalists
that are currently working inside Russia,

00:05:18.718 --> 00:05:21.921
including Americans,
including you know, we have colleagues

00:05:22.155 --> 00:05:24.490
who maybe not from America,
but other Western countries

00:05:24.724 --> 00:05:26.426
reporting from Russia as well.

00:05:26.426 --> 00:05:29.996
Is the administration's take
now that they should leave?

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:33.933
We can't speak for other countries
and certainly wouldn't do that.

00:05:34.133 --> 00:05:37.070
Those are those are sovereign
nation states

00:05:37.070 --> 00:05:38.971
that can speak for their own citizens.

00:05:38.971 --> 00:05:40.206
And we would leave it at that.

00:05:40.206 --> 00:05:43.676
What we're saying is and the State
Department's been extremely clear

00:05:43.676 --> 00:05:46.579
about this on their website,
they've got a level four advisory out.

00:05:47.046 --> 00:05:50.850
Russia is not a safe country
for Americans to travel to or to be.

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:54.120
And if you are in Russia, again,
we urge you to leave immediately.

00:05:54.887 --> 00:05:59.992
You have said that you do not know if this
detention was retaliatory or perhaps.

00:06:00.426 --> 00:06:04.130
Vladimir Putin seeking a prisoner swap,
which he's been known to do in the past.

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:07.567
Many experts who follow him
believe that's, in fact, part of his plan

00:06:07.567 --> 00:06:08.568
right now.

00:06:08.568 --> 00:06:10.737
What is the US's view on this?

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:12.271
Is there anybody that the U.S.

00:06:12.271 --> 00:06:17.610
is currently detaining who would be able
to be swapped with with Evan?

00:06:18.277 --> 00:06:20.313
We don't know exactly

00:06:20.780 --> 00:06:23.483
what other motives
beyond what they've said publicly

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:26.786
for arresting and detaining.

00:06:26.786 --> 00:06:29.622
Evan is we just
we don't have any evidence that this was

00:06:29.622 --> 00:06:33.826
some sort of retaliatory measure
or that it is, in fact, a ploy by Mr.

00:06:33.826 --> 00:06:35.495
Putin to do a prisoner swap.

00:06:35.495 --> 00:06:37.930
And I won't get ahead of where we are
on the process here.

00:06:37.930 --> 00:06:41.968
We're going to work to get Evan released,
just like we're going to work to get Paul

00:06:41.968 --> 00:06:45.638
Whalen released
and any other detained Americans overseas.

00:06:45.738 --> 00:06:47.073
Each case is individual.

00:06:47.073 --> 00:06:49.075
Each case is specific.

00:06:49.075 --> 00:06:52.412
And so I certainly wouldn't talk
about what tactics might be in play

00:06:52.412 --> 00:06:54.247
or what options are before us

00:06:54.247 --> 00:06:57.350
as we continue to try to work to learn
more about Evan's case.

00:06:57.383 --> 00:07:00.620
Our main priority right now, obviously,
we'd like to see him released right now.

00:07:00.620 --> 00:07:02.221
Of course, he doesn't need to be detained.

00:07:02.221 --> 00:07:05.792
But our main priority is getting access
to him physically, consular access

00:07:06.025 --> 00:07:06.993
so we can ascertain

00:07:06.993 --> 00:07:10.563
how he's doing and and try to address
any immediate needs that he might have.

00:07:11.097 --> 00:07:13.132
Do you have any developments?
Please do keep us posted.

00:07:13.166 --> 00:07:15.401
I do want to move on to the war
in Ukraine in general,

00:07:15.401 --> 00:07:19.272
because there is growing concern
about what, in fact, the U.S.

00:07:19.272 --> 00:07:23.576
policy is vis-a-vis
the war in Ukraine from the get-Go.

00:07:23.643 --> 00:07:28.147
The Biden administration has said
that it is about liberating Ukraine

00:07:28.147 --> 00:07:31.784
and making sure
Russia leaves its boundaries there

00:07:31.784 --> 00:07:34.620
and nothing would be done
without Ukraine involved.

00:07:34.887 --> 00:07:38.858
That having been said,
there is speculation that going forward

00:07:38.858 --> 00:07:43.129
and any sort of assistance in policy
really depends a lot on this upcoming

00:07:43.129 --> 00:07:46.265
offensive that is expected from Ukraine.

00:07:46.265 --> 00:07:48.134
Is that in fact the case?

00:07:48.134 --> 00:07:51.103
How important and pivotal will this

00:07:51.103 --> 00:07:54.273
upcoming offensive be in the decision
making process?

00:07:54.841 --> 00:07:58.377
I do not want to speak for future
operations of the Ukrainian military.

00:07:58.411 --> 00:07:59.145
I would never do that.

00:07:59.145 --> 00:08:01.514
I wouldn't even do that
for American future operations.

00:08:02.114 --> 00:08:04.951
We do expect that the Russians
are going to go on the offense here,

00:08:05.384 --> 00:08:08.554
try to go on the offense here
in weeks and months ahead, and it's likely

00:08:08.554 --> 00:08:12.158
that the fighting will get more vicious
and more bloodily more bloody.

00:08:12.325 --> 00:08:15.228
We want to make sure that the Ukrainians
are able to defend themselves

00:08:15.228 --> 00:08:17.897
against what we anticipate
will be Russian offensive operations.

00:08:17.897 --> 00:08:19.332
And if they choose

00:08:19.332 --> 00:08:22.869
to be able to successfully conduct
offensive operations of their own.

00:08:22.869 --> 00:08:26.939
And so that's what's been behind all these
recent packages of support we provided.

00:08:26.939 --> 00:08:29.242
You've seen a lot of ammunition
going in in recent weeks.

00:08:29.408 --> 00:08:30.543
You'll continue to see that.

00:08:30.543 --> 00:08:33.212
We want to make sure that they're ready
for those offensive operations

00:08:33.212 --> 00:08:34.413
if they choose to conduct.

00:08:34.413 --> 00:08:37.984
And, John, just to be clear, it's
the Ukrainian offensive

00:08:38.117 --> 00:08:41.287
that I was actually referring to that
that's expected in the spring,

00:08:41.287 --> 00:08:42.788
in the coming weeks ahead.

00:08:42.788 --> 00:08:46.225
How much is riding on Ukraine's success
in terms of

00:08:46.225 --> 00:08:49.295
what position the Biden administration
takes moving forward?

00:08:49.328 --> 00:08:50.263
Right. No, no,

00:08:50.263 --> 00:08:53.466
I definitely understood the question
and what I don't want to talk about.

00:08:54.033 --> 00:08:57.003
Any potential offensive operations
conducted by the Ukrainians,

00:08:57.003 --> 00:08:59.071
that's for them to decide
and for them to speak to

00:08:59.071 --> 00:09:01.541
We just want to make sure
that they're ready to defend themselves.

00:09:01.541 --> 00:09:04.710
And if they choose to go on the offense,
to do it and do it successfully.

00:09:04.710 --> 00:09:05.811
And that's the key point.

00:09:05.811 --> 00:09:09.115
We want them to be successful
on the battlefield so that if

00:09:09.115 --> 00:09:13.085
and when President Zelensky is ready to
sit down at the negotiating table with Mr.

00:09:13.085 --> 00:09:14.987
Putin and there's no signs that
that's in the offing

00:09:14.987 --> 00:09:19.058
any time soon that he can be successful
at the negotiating table, too.

00:09:19.058 --> 00:09:22.862
We want him to have as much strength
going into those discussions

00:09:23.095 --> 00:09:24.130
as humanly possible.

00:09:24.130 --> 00:09:27.333
That's why we're focused on making sure
that the Ukrainians continue to be

00:09:27.333 --> 00:09:31.737
and beyond they have been extraordinarily
successful on the battlefield.

00:09:31.804 --> 00:09:32.171
You know,

00:09:32.171 --> 00:09:34.674
they've clawed back
more than 50% of the territory

00:09:34.674 --> 00:09:37.343
that Russia took for them
in the early weeks and months of this war.

00:09:37.443 --> 00:09:39.211
We want to see that success continue.

00:09:39.211 --> 00:09:42.315
And that's what we're focused on
is the administration.

00:09:42.315 --> 00:09:46.953
And final question, factoring in perhaps
the possibility that Vladimir Putin never

00:09:46.953 --> 00:09:50.556
wants to sit down at the negotiating
go go shouting table earnestly, at least.

00:09:50.890 --> 00:09:53.025
He certainly has shown
no indication of that, has he?

00:09:53.025 --> 00:09:56.329
I mean, every everything
that he has been doing, just matching

00:09:56.829 --> 00:09:59.098
his actions instead of his words.

00:09:59.098 --> 00:10:01.634
I mean, everything you can see is
he wants to continue this war.

00:10:01.634 --> 00:10:05.471
He wants to continue to to take away
Ukraine's independence, their sovereignty.

00:10:05.471 --> 00:10:09.542
He wants to subsume Ukraine into Russia,
doesn't want them to exist anymore.

00:10:09.542 --> 00:10:12.044
And the Ukrainians are fighting literally
for their independence.

00:10:12.211 --> 00:10:13.579
We see no signs that Mr.

00:10:13.579 --> 00:10:18.417
Putin is willing to slack off back offer
or sit down and have any discussions.

00:10:18.851 --> 00:10:20.519
And you know what?

00:10:20.519 --> 00:10:23.589
We'd all love to see the war end
certainly as soon as possible.

00:10:23.756 --> 00:10:26.859
And if it has to end to a negotiated
settlement, as you rightly said,

00:10:27.293 --> 00:10:29.862
when we started talking
nothing about Ukraine without Ukraine.

00:10:29.862 --> 00:10:31.897
Ukraine's got to be at the center
of that discussion.

00:10:31.897 --> 00:10:33.132
They've got to be consulted.

00:10:33.132 --> 00:10:35.901
Their perspectives
have to be viewed and understood.

00:10:36.235 --> 00:10:37.069
But Mr.

00:10:37.069 --> 00:10:40.172
Putin could end this war today
just by pulling his troops out of Ukraine.

00:10:40.339 --> 00:10:42.141
Again, he's shown no signs of doing that,

00:10:42.141 --> 00:10:44.777
which is why we've got to continue
to support Ukraine on the battlefield.

00:10:45.511 --> 00:10:47.446
All right, John Kirby,
thank you so much for your time.

00:10:47.446 --> 00:10:48.948
We appreciate it. You bet.

